{"title":"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#In_Chinese,subtitle_in_English,中文解说\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">In Chinese,subtitle in English,中文解说</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all composite integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> that satisfy the following property: if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b935808e571b8054beca04324e72b7d39c53a00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1,d_2,\\dots,d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> are all the positive divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e5f12a74bd69e4381fcf44aa1d37f1c1f17e5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=d_1&lt;d_2&lt;\\dots&lt;d_k=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"216\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/7/7775e33f3677b0b131dcd51dfd58106aa1829825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{i+1}+d_{i+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e1e6ddfc11e72523c0cdc09c5bcd49fa3497388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le i \\le k-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JhThDz0H7cI\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JhThDz0H7cI</a> [Video contains solutions to all day 1 problems]\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FBwvqDUEDFc?si=DYrxR9wI1YaKvDm-\">https://youtu.be/FBwvqDUEDFc?si=DYrxR9wI1YaKvDm-</a> [Video contains IMO 2023 P1 motivation + discussion] (~little-fermat)\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/sQjqjCMcetU\">https://youtu.be/sQjqjCMcetU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"In_Chinese.2Csubtitle_in_English.2C.E4.B8.AD.E6.96.87.E8.A7.A3.E8.AF.B4\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"In_Chinese,subtitle_in_English,中文解说\">In Chinese,subtitle in English,中文解说</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: In Chinese,subtitle in English,中文解说\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/USvm7R-g6wo\">https://youtu.be/USvm7R-g6wo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> has at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> prime divisors, WLOG let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8b1b4a0b8eb1df6ee52c2d040401d9dda8e78df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&lt;q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> be the smallest two of these primes. Then the ordered tuple of divisors is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5289517ccc99857c035061bb809b5641f40f64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,\\,  p,\\,  p^2 \\dots,\\,  p^a,\\,  q \\dots,\\,  n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"21\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261483393788c1276a45334b5f5a196dae556b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>To prove this claim, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the smallest prime that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, so it is the smallest divisor not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, meaning the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divisors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Furthermore, the smallest divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that is not equal to a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (i.e. not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1dfb0db3c1d7fc6b06331308e7ecc7322ec14566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,\\, p,\\, p^2\\dots)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. This is because all other divisors either include a prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> different from both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, which is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are the smallest two prime divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />), or don’t include a different prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. In the first case, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7015f89125e50437bf1f1b02f3aec84d7f0d0e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, the divisor is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. In the second case, all divisors divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88bb97ca2ab6cdd3823e982b86f796662e4a58c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> are also larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and otherwise are of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d4ebe00d4e02cca16e594ecd90b2fcd6e7b97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^x \\cdot q^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc648593247e70f010b99b0b05d4c8e37b25613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> for some nonnegative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. If the divisor is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc648593247e70f010b99b0b05d4c8e37b25613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" />, then it is a power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. If it is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d4ebe00d4e02cca16e594ecd90b2fcd6e7b97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^x \\cdot q^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"20\" />, the smallest of these factors is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/c/aaca71ad6460f92d2c5700e3722a1eef261e0d81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^0 \\cdot q^1 = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, (in the case where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or more primes divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />) the ordered tuple of divisors is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5289517ccc99857c035061bb809b5641f40f64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,\\,  p,\\,  p^2 \\dots,\\,  p^a,\\,  q \\dots,\\,  n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"21\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261483393788c1276a45334b5f5a196dae556b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, since after each divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/c/7bc648593247e70f010b99b0b05d4c8e37b25613.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" />, the next smallest divisor is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/c/c5cf6d2ba43b3965a655505080367ce07948c7dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> or simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff258ccdd14498ab730507a5cf8d5d10c33626d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />, the condition fails. This is because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/583508a6728df7e4862ca47949c9cf690eeb711b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{a-1} \\nmid p^a + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"21\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/f/87f51eac5a26058404c9965071d007662993d8e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"18\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e20a36b4f7b71b87c38490d6df15a6984e5d69e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{a-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not since it is a prime different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547b180f03f6f367de2b2b97c462819497b6b50b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{a-1}=p^0=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />, which does divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> for the condition to be satisfied in this case. However, we know that the ordered list of divisors satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6dca3605cf2dc13d4569b554fa1eb551e434968.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i \\cdot d_{k+1-i}=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, meaning since the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divisors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/2131fa6a345cdedce081b3849f948dddbc83be08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, p, q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />, then the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> divisors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d58bbcd2672ce97017043696623559cac5b380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{n}{q}, \\frac{n}{p}, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/3/7a317e52d39e3d16a3c5e64df4fc8247076331dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{n}{q})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"31\" height=\"38\" /> must divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c07271ed065d1150db08469e9e6649eca012cd56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{n}{p} + n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a6bb689ce31bd42a5bb81d4ebc6d8138e13c242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"17\" height=\"38\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3ce208f6ea3ba5f69308384e93b2951af0ebe90c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{p} + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> must also be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, but since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502e059d1a020b368aee3a99c5669d88331d321f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091baae5b6049afb17b051f6a27b655b92ed34de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"17\" height=\"38\" /> is and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> isn't.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/a/8fae72ac8efa25964a89c7e5426a786efc4720d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=p^x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, it is easy to verify this works for all primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/8341d1cdc5d4b2c87ebf34b409a7c7fe5b15cd36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf78f61c0d0caf962f08883b16667268459b0a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^y  \\vert  p^{y+1} + p^{y+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"21\" />, and the divisors are ordered as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0cff29b4f95c151220a1ef580027da055cbaa66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1,\\, p,\\, p^2…\\, p^x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>~SpencerD,K kai, Najeeb the math genius\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar argument as above but restated.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/794f075d57bf61f48b00acbc2507763911143cfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = p_1^{e_1} p_2^{d_2} \\dots p_k^{e_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"134\" height=\"22\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed44e843be43102f5549381b57508df1f2578a24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1 &lt; p_2 &lt; \\dots &lt; p_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" /> primes. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, it's easy to verify that this property holds, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb6f57023bed84267ba83e1d900537f642c5e89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^l \\mid p^{l+1} + p^{l+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. All divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> which contain a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/4508393135451dc6c41b01f36072dd16674586bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"11\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> is at least as large as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8bc2235f5b0094bc37f2ef74f7dc647f0a406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />. So, the only divisors which are possibly less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8bc2235f5b0094bc37f2ef74f7dc647f0a406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> are of the form  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/b/86ba7da77a97969c40dc7cac89bc35135b862dad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1^{j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"22\" />. Also, by construction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01486dcc7cb25518b89692706b17389dc67c92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8bc2235f5b0094bc37f2ef74f7dc647f0a406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />. Putting it all together, this says that the smallest factors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1523f278055fb3d838c525998baf2f8524d89b70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, p_1, \\dots, p_1^j, p_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f2a96e7072077edc5b2058d152eeeab9a54d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/5140edf4a6136ae9cbef968278ad286ec668653f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934402be8eb742a21250726bf445d5e386790a33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1^{j-1} \\nmid p_1^j + p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"23\" />, since the LHS has a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01486dcc7cb25518b89692706b17389dc67c92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> and the RHS does not since.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/e/39e0ea623f4a7b3cbe6b70ca8b063ccfee0ddb51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, then the largest three factors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/108c94721e2d9d72e8e4848cb6c29bd759c317a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{n}{p_2}, \\frac{n}{p_1}, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/762b1cae6880055af70ca71d2a5758e24bfbdf25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{p_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> have a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/f/0ef3615fdf494726ad8d59ade88d88f214fc5cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1^{e_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"19\" />, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a9712be145ce0ab0733d7ba4044a6d65bbf88be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{p_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"19\" height=\"36\" /> only has a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9889fd89f0b475e30201e7f01f4182a90e144e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1^{e_1 - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8b1fe5ad6dc6de8dd32d58305fbb9b49efedca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{p_2} \\nmid \\frac{n}{p_1} + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Hence the prime powers are the only composite numbers which satisfy the property.\n~kislay kai approved\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/947f2942e21473c0db4a0b93675f7b805785a067.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=p_1\\cdots p_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" /> be the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/745bb27bd3558d6e79b75147dbad53441e3e4359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1\\leq p_2 \\leq \\cdots \\leq p_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />. We will show <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9cb9ff657de3cbe3341902f8f6ce02ed73dba3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1=\\cdots = p_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffb57c92ea3c844c52e8449e2195d716c9c36707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1 | d_2 | \\cdots | d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" /> by induction on the property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e9eceb5c805a272e59cd35fc0cb0df9c5831c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> below. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/b/a4b5800f5ad040d308609190ef18a9e0ca08a9b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> there's nothing to show. Therefore let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6fa6546da3adb7c8422b7d96a499c43757390c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e9eceb5c805a272e59cd35fc0cb0df9c5831c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/1736126071b6e547b317b780a88e0e405ca26881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> be the properties\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d966d975d145f0102f1afa8c36f76ace0311a78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp;d_{k-i} | d_{k-i+2} | \\cdots | d_k \\\\ &amp;p_1 = p_2 = \\cdots = p_i. \\end{align*}\" width=\"146\" height=\"42\" />\nThese conditions clearly imply (by induction) that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787a176965760d1a8866a6f1645f9c9ea1ebc3fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_{k-j} = p_1^{i-j} p_{i+1} \\cdots p_m \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (1)\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"22\" />\nfor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/b/74b147dcac92e899e358fff8d9239513ae57811c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq j \\leq i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>Base case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/1079eb7c4fc10d5c411bd0524a7f1f8c65a058f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" />: \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a728486767e8770683066decc7e51900e8c7fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-2}|d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d14bc4608651bc2844d57843a35aa17bfeeb639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-2}|d_{k-1}+d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" /> it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72014e4361e5113b6b49f1f49261c2d9cb8aab5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-2}|d_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />. Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e070755b421b446388913499bebd9425cf2380e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-1}|d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />. Also note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3ab7b8d227f0f8732bb2783e1afb7b8bcf28db8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-1} = p_2 \\cdots p_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448bf8054dc47dc879958ff386a95793e8690877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> is the largest divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> not equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Now, since all divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448bf8054dc47dc879958ff386a95793e8690877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b2568d0ec56197b67179189b9ff539ba61e6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> (which divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448bf8054dc47dc879958ff386a95793e8690877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />) is the largest divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448bf8054dc47dc879958ff386a95793e8690877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />, it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/8803bdfcb4b2af6baf076b9b00de611bcf4f48e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-2} = p_3 \\cdots p_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> (or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/9/94963eaf5cbc0f7a9cfca22f91d560c85d0ae270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-2}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3eaf8047a3f5bebfc5c43e27123a15a44d7540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=2$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />). Now, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/7441df54eeb962296c5f93234ccd7deee9a328c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1&lt;p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c9de9bf07ebdb32b5270ae1e9c6012113b62d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l=p_1p_3\\cdots p_m &gt; d_{k-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" /> and divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, but doesn't equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448bf8054dc47dc879958ff386a95793e8690877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d09bd8dc83be3b4a1bc205b9cc6fa40b23c7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />. A contradiction. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b8652a9653928e31a4ac166eca4558ed90a5b8d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1=p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75d81224803b226673999612682924da1823f760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(i+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />: \n</p><p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e9eceb5c805a272e59cd35fc0cb0df9c5831c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4185ff170df7c7c31c0e728d69b152ea86683013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\leq i &lt; k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28f4853da3e906458f4dd120989bf2b5452b0a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-i-1} | d_{k-i}+d_{k-i+1} = p_{i+1}\\cdots p_m + p_1p_{i+1}\\cdots p_m = d_{k-i}(1+p_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"504\" height=\"20\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. Now, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f966857fcec32d2ddcbce1258dc0277a479fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-i-1}|p_1\\cdots p_m=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" /> but no factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462ae0c1b6183bee640d21163c15915de130a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />, it follows\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1c763b3e885528f63dc3f8df134912987ed26de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_{k-i-1}|d_{k-i}.\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />   \nFurthermore, since all factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12badf2984fa2224145c9a8d499cb94301cb37a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> divide of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/4/2e474b2fb1c8adfcecc0ab901798710e7a931e5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-i-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> is the largest divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351ac872db6dee5c13891c6d16bb9aa13ce98bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-i}=p_{i+1}\\cdots p_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />, it follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/293eb369c195b18fb71b37e7ad9fe2f2db17ca98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-i-1} = p_{i+2} \\cdots p_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" /> (or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a34ca1ec57c6726333b930125505e5d9397b1093.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-i-1} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/5087e61d3f438651d11083da3f507a9ffdf21e4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=k-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" />). Now, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3ff0a61d6092cc4c03cdbb46eb368405a546f8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{i+1}&gt;p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> then \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e958870b8e69b1cb5cf6bd1fccbd83b6286f894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l=p_1p_{i+2}\\cdots p_m &gt; d_{k-i-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"203\" height=\"18\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> but doesn't equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0bad068af2b2fba1e694f49c69217e6168b2fe6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{k-i}, d_{k-i+1},...,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d09bd8dc83be3b4a1bc205b9cc6fa40b23c7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />. A contradiction. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c04f40cd35dcb02d9678198047d0f120532a8bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_{i+1}=p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />. This completes the induction. \n</p><p>It follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cfcc84c34efa0f77662d00a1ed6c851f84227b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(k-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> holds, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/3362c41f666b5918bae9937665d4589799ce3eb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=d_k = p_1^{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"22\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87ef70436c3459e4122948de97214d3a2dc061b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />. On the other hand this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> satisfies the criteria.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO\" title=\"2023 IMO\">2023 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018023633\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.064 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 889/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 30470/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.801      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.801      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24782:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018023633 and revision id 283450. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}